# Stopwatch and pomodoro

Two timers built the same way: a component-owned `Every 1 second as tick:`
that never itself stops, guarded by a `running` field so "pause" and
"resume" are just that field. `Stop the timer tick.` and `Start the timer
tick.` would pause and resume the timer itself; the field keeps the timer
untouched and the state in one place a test can read.

## To pad2 (n: Int) -> Text:
    If n is less than 10:
        Return "0{n}".
    Return "{n}".

## To formatTime (totalSeconds: Int) -> Text:
    Let minutes be totalSeconds / 60.
    Let secs be totalSeconds % 60.
    Return "{pad2(minutes)}:{pad2(secs)}".

## Component Stopwatch

State:
    Let seconds be 0.
    Let running be false.

Actions:
    Every 1 second as tick:
        If running:
            Set seconds to seconds + 1.

    To start:
        Set running to true.

    To pause:
        Set running to false.

    To reset:
        Set running to false.
        Set seconds to 0.

View:
    <div class="stopwatch card">
      <p id="sw-time">{formatTime(seconds)}</p>
      <button id="sw-start" on-click={start}>Start</button>
      <button id="sw-pause" on-click={pause}>Pause</button>
      <button id="sw-reset" on-click={reset}>Reset</button>
    </div>

## Note

The pomodoro counts down from 5 seconds rather than the traditional 25
minutes, so `Advance time by ... seconds.` can drive a whole session
deterministically in a test — the mechanics (start, pause, reach zero, the
`done` flag) are identical at any length.

## Component Pomodoro

State:
    Let remaining be 5.
    Let running be false.
    Let done be false.

Actions:
    Every 1 second as tick:
        If running:
            If remaining is greater than 0:
                Set remaining to remaining - 1.
                If remaining is equal to 0:
                    Set running to false.
                    Set done to true.

    To start:
        Set running to true.
        Set done to false.

    To pause:
        Set running to false.

    To reset:
        Set running to false.
        Set done to false.
        Set remaining to 5.

View:
    <div class="pomodoro">
      <p id="pd-time">{formatTime(remaining)}</p>
      <button id="pd-start" on-click={start}>Start</button>
      <button id="pd-pause" on-click={pause}>Pause</button>
      <button id="pd-reset" on-click={reset}>Reset</button>
      {if done:}<p id="pd-done">Time's up!</p>{end}
    </div>

## Page /

View:
    <main class="timers">
      <h1>Stopwatch</h1>
      <Stopwatch/>
      <h1>Pomodoro</h1>
      <Pomodoro/>
    </main>

Style:
    .timers p { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: 2rem; }

## Test: the stopwatch starts at zero and does not move on its own

Expect that the text of "#sw-time" is equal to "00:00".
Advance time by 3 seconds.
Expect that the text of "#sw-time" is equal to "00:00".

## Test: starting the stopwatch counts seconds, pausing holds them

Click "#sw-start".
Advance time by 3 seconds.
Expect that the text of "#sw-time" is equal to "00:03".
Click "#sw-pause".
Advance time by 5 seconds.
Expect that the text of "#sw-time" is equal to "00:03".

## Test: resuming continues from where it paused

Click "#sw-start".
Advance time by 2 seconds.
Click "#sw-pause".
Click "#sw-start".
Advance time by 2 seconds.
Expect that the text of "#sw-time" is equal to "00:04".

## Test: resetting the stopwatch stops it and zeroes the display

Click "#sw-start".
Advance time by 4 seconds.
Click "#sw-reset".
Expect that the text of "#sw-time" is equal to "00:00".
Advance time by 4 seconds.
Expect that the text of "#sw-time" is equal to "00:00".

## Test: the pomodoro counts down and announces when it finishes

Expect that the text of "#pd-time" is equal to "00:05".
Click "#pd-start".
Advance time by 5 seconds.
Expect that the text of "#pd-time" is equal to "00:00".
Expect that the text of "#pd-done" is equal to "Time's up!".

## Test: pausing the pomodoro holds the remaining time

Click "#pd-start".
Advance time by 2 seconds.
Click "#pd-pause".
Advance time by 5 seconds.
Expect that the text of "#pd-time" is equal to "00:03".
Expect that "#pd-done" is hidden.

## Test: resetting the pomodoro returns to the full duration

Click "#pd-start".
Advance time by 5 seconds.
Click "#pd-reset".
Expect that the text of "#pd-time" is equal to "00:05".
Expect that "#pd-done" is hidden.
